db.sqlite3
# The lock file of the mail sender sits next to the database (plan §11.7).
# Deliberately **without** a leading slash: the database path is freely configurable through
# DEMOCKRAZY_DB_PATH, and the lock file follows it. This is the exception to the lesson from B18 --
# there the missing anchoring was the bug, here it is the intent.
*.mailsend.lock

# This means STATIC_ROOT, so the collectstatic output under BASE_DIR/static -- which is why the leading
# slash limits it to the project root. Without the slash the pattern matches every directory named
# "static" at every level, so vote/static/ with the app's source assets as well. That is exactly what it
# did from 2016 to 2026 (see B18): only the two files older than the rule were tracked there, and every
# new asset silently fell out.
/static/

.direnv

# Lokale Claude-Code-Konfiguration (Berechtigungen, Startbefehle) -- gehoert nicht ins Repo.
.claude/
